# Supabase migrations — RLS required

Every migration that creates or alters a **user-facing** `public` table must include Row Level Security.

## Checklist (each new/changed table)

1. `ALTER TABLE ... ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;`
2. At least one policy per operation the app uses (`SELECT`, `INSERT`, `UPDATE`, `DELETE`).
3. Default-deny: no broad `USING (true)` unless documented (e.g. read-only reference data).
4. Use helpers from `002_roles_and_admin.sql` when staff access is needed:
   - `public.has_min_role('admin')` — admin + developer
   - `public.is_developer()` — developer only
   - `auth.uid() = user_id` — end-user owns row
5. `DROP POLICY IF EXISTS ...` before `CREATE POLICY` when replacing policies.
6. `service_role` bypasses RLS — never rely on it from the extension; Edge Functions only.

## Role hierarchy

`user` < `admin` < `developer` (developer highest).

| Role | Typical access |
|------|----------------|
| user | Own rows only |
| admin | Read cross-user metadata; manage licenses; audit log |
| developer | Full data + role assignment |

## E2EE reminder

Cloud rows store **ciphertext** only. Admin policies allow metadata reads, not plaintext CV (client-decrypted).

## New migration file naming

`supabase/migrations/NNN_description.sql` — run with `npm run db:migrate`.

## After every migration

1. Update [supabase-schema.mdc](supabase-schema.mdc) — ER diagram + table list must match SQL.
2. Note new `sync_documents.doc_key` values in that file if the extension gains settings.
